Create a new target in the nearest targ file.

Usage:
  targ --create [group...] <name> [flags...] "<shell-command>"

Formats:
  duration  <int><unit> where unit is s (seconds), m (minutes), h (hours)

Positionals:
  <group...>
  <name> (required)
  "<shell-command>" (required)

Flags:
  --deps <targets...>         Deps to run first
  --cache <patterns...>       Skip if unchanged
  --watch <patterns...>       Re-run on change
  --timeout <duration>        Execution timeout
  --times <n>                 Run n times
  --retry                     Continue on failure
  --backoff <duration,mult>   Backoff (1s,2.0)
  --dep-mode <mode>           serial or parallel

Examples:
  targ --create test "go test ./..."
  targ --create dev lint --deps fmt --cache "**/*.go" "golangci-lint run"
  targ --create test --timeout 30s --retry "go test ./..."
